{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01311",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.0,
      "end_seconds": 7.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.98,
      "end_seconds": 11.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.93,
      "end_seconds": 17.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Doctor, um, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.18,
      "end_seconds": 23.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 25.06,
      "end_seconds": 32.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "Doctor, it's an itchy patch on my wrist. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.78,
      "end_seconds": 36.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.18,
      "end_seconds": 40.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "It's been five days, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.55,
      "end_seconds": 50.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.04,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.29,
      "end_seconds": 59.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "My new watch strap definitely sets it off. It happens a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.64,
      "end_seconds": 66.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 66.49,
      "end_seconds": 73.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Well, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.12,
      "end_seconds": 90.84,
      "duration_seconds": 15.72,
      "text": "Erm, I was getting to that! Oh, you know, and a bit of redness. That's been about the same, about a week. There was dry flaky skin, yes, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.06,
      "end_seconds": 98.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "Have you had an itchy patch on your wrist before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.81,
      "end_seconds": 110.29,
      "duration_seconds": 10.48,
      "text": "Erm, yes, something like this happened a couple of years ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.35,
      "end_seconds": 112.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.65,
      "end_seconds": 115.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "No fever, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 115.96,
      "end_seconds": 121.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.86,
      "end_seconds": 129.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "Yeah, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.36,
      "end_seconds": 138.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any blisters or spreading at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.42,
      "end_seconds": 142.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.19,
      "end_seconds": 148.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.14,
      "end_seconds": 154.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.81,
      "end_seconds": 160.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.58,
      "end_seconds": 171.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "I have depression, for two years. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.5,
      "end_seconds": 173.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Yes, carry on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.99,
      "end_seconds": 181.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "I, I have COPD. I've had migraines for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.08,
      "end_seconds": 183.05,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.67,
      "end_seconds": 185.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.3,
      "end_seconds": 190.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.45,
      "end_seconds": 193.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.85,
      "end_seconds": 198.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.77,
      "end_seconds": 202.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.65,
      "end_seconds": 207.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.15,
      "end_seconds": 212.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.87,
      "end_seconds": 218.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.7,
      "end_seconds": 223.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.31,
      "end_seconds": 231.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Ah, my daughter has type 1 diabetes. My grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.31,
      "end_seconds": 236.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.67,
      "end_seconds": 241.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 243.54,
      "end_seconds": 250.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.22,
      "text": "It's meant to be when needed, though I don't see she take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.62,
      "end_seconds": 275.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Right, are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.19,
      "end_seconds": 282.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Not currently, but as a youngster erythromycin gave me a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.78,
      "end_seconds": 294.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.46,
      "end_seconds": 300.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 301.83,
      "end_seconds": 310.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse 83, BP is 111 over 74, respiratory rate 15, temp 36.9 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.05,
      "end_seconds": 312.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.94,
      "end_seconds": 318.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.04,
      "end_seconds": 322.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.08,
      "end_seconds": 339.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "There's a neat red patch where the watch strap sits, with a little scaling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.77,
      "end_seconds": 353.46,
      "duration_seconds": 11.69,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So where does that leave us? My working impression is mild contact dermatitis from the watch strap. I'd also keep eczema in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.99,
      "end_seconds": 357.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "So, what are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.87,
      "end_seconds": 386.33,
      "duration_seconds": 27.46,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's mild contact dermatitis from the watch strap, and we'll watch how it goes. We'll begin with hydrocortisone cream, 1%, once a day, one week. That's for contact dermatitis. Stop wearing that strap and keep the skin moisturised. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 386.96,
      "end_seconds": 389.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.9,
      "end_seconds": 392.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}